<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Adaptive launcher icon — foreground layer (TASK-12, FR-41 / OQ-05).

    A "foglio" (sheet) mark: one filled path, drawn in the canon brand DARK token over the brand
    LIGHT background. The ink references `@color/brand_brown` (S11) instead of restating #873000,
    so the mark, the palette resource and the icon test can never drift apart.

    The ruled lines and the folded corner are carved out of the same path with fillType="evenOdd"
    (API 24+, minSdk 26), so the mark is genuinely transparent — it never paints over the
    background layer and stays correct if the background variant changes.

    Geometry is kept inside the 66dp adaptive-icon safe circle (centre 54,54; radius 33) so no
    launcher mask (circle, squircle, rounded square) clips the sheet: corners at (37,28) and
    (71,80) sit at 31.1dp from centre.

    This vector doubles as the <monochrome> layer of both adaptive icons: a monochrome layer is
    consumed as an alpha mask and tinted by the system, so the mark's shape (including the carved
    rules) is exactly what a themed icon needs, with no duplicated geometry.

    CANON GAP: ui-design-bible §Iconography documents the in-app symbolic icon set only — it
    carries no launcher/mark specification. This vector is therefore a faithful derivation of the
    existing Foglietto sheet identity per OQ-05, not a traced canon asset; final icon production
    belongs to the later Play wave.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/brand_brown"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M37,28 L60,28 L71,39 L71,80 L37,80 Z M60,28 L71,39 L60,39 Z M44,44 L64,44 L64,49 L44,49 Z M44,55 L64,55 L64,60 L44,60 Z M44,66 L58,66 L58,71 L44,71 Z" />
</vector>
